{{also|turr|yurr}}
==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|is|non|þurr}}, from {{inh|is|gem-pro|*þursuz}}, from {{inh|is|ine-pro|*ters-}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|is|/θʏrː/}}
*: {{rhymes|is|ʏrː|s=1}}

===Adjective===
{{is-adj|þurrari|þurrastur}}

# [[dry]]; without [[liquid]]
# {{lb|is|informal}} [[dry]], [[alcohol-free]]; without [[alcohol]]
#: ''Þetta var '''þurr''' helgi.''
#:: It was an '''alcohol-free''' weekend.

====Inflection====
{{is-decl-adj-1|þ|u|rr}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|is|þurr á manninn}} (brusque)
* {{l|is|upp úr þurru}} (suddenly, out of nothing, unprovoked)

